                                  </ul>
          <div class="tab-content p-md-4 border border-top-0 rounded-2 rounded-top-0">
            <div class="tab-pane active" id="tab-description"><div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">Prohibited by the manufacturer Rockchip, we're not allowed to ship this product, or to provide any tech support, to the following countries/regions: Russia, Belarus, Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, Crimea, Donetsk and Luhansk regions of Ukraine. (Countries or regions are subject to change based on updates or revisions to export control regulations)</div>
<div class="itemDesc">
  <div class="richWrap">
		
  	<div class="pdT" style="background: #19243a; color: #ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle" style="font-size: 3em;"><strong>Luckfox Pico Pi</strong></div>
      <p class="alignl pdTRBL2">
			The <strong>Luckfox Pico Pi</strong> is a cost-effective Linux micro development board, based on the Luckfox Core1106 chip to provide a simple and efficient development platform for developers. Supports a variety of interfaces including MIPI CSI, GPIO, UART, SPI, I2C, USB, and an M.2 slot for 4G module, etc., which is ideal for a wide range of embedded applications.
			</p>
      <img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-1.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, front view" class="lazyload">
	  <img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-3.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, features" class="lazyload">
    </div>
	  
  	<div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Development Board Versions</div>
      <img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-5.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, version options" class="lazyload">
    </div>
	  
	  <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color: #fff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Version Comparison</div>
    	<table class="tabSty-2 mgnTB alignc" style="background: #000000; color: #fff;">
    <tbody><tr>
      <th style="background: #000000; width: 30%;">Model</th>
      <td>Luckfox Pico Pi A</td>
      <td>Luckfox Pico Pi B</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th style="background: #000000;">Processor</th>
      <td>RV1106G3</td>
      <td>RV1106G2</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	  <th style="background: #000000;">NPU</th>
      <td>1TOPS</td>
      <td>0.5TOPS</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
	  <th style="background: #000000;">Memory</th>
      <td>256MB DDR3L</td>
      <td>128MB DDR3L</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody></table>
<br>
 </div> 
	  
  	<div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">SIM7600G-H-M.2</div>
		<p class="alignl pdTRBL">The SIM7600G-H-M.2 is a LTE Cat 4 module which supports wireless communication modes of LTE-TDD, LTE-FDD, HSPA+, GSM, GPRS, and EDGE, etc. It adopts M.2 form factor and can be integrated into the Luckfox Pico Pi series</p>
      <img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-7.jpg" alt="SIM7600G-H-M.2 4G module, front and back view" class="lazyload">
    </div>
	  
	  
	   <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color: #ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Wi-Fi 6 and Bluetooth module</div>
      <p class="richDesc pdTRBL">
				Onboard 2.4GHz Wi-Fi 6 and Bluetooth 5.2/BLE Bluetooth Module, Providing Stable Connection And Efficient Transmission
			</p>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-13.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard Wi-Fi 6 and Bluetooth module" class="lazyload">
		</div>
	  
	  <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Reserved PoE Module Header</div>
      <p class="richDesc">
				More Flexible for Power Supply
			</p>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-15.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard reserved PoE module header" class="lazyload">
			 <p class="note">
				* the PoE module is NOT included.
			</p>
		</div>
	  
	  <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Onboard TF card slot</div>
      <p class="richDesc">
				allows storage expansion via TF card
			</p>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-17.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard TF card slot" class="lazyload">
			 <p class="note">
				* Supports storage expansion only, does not support booting system from TF card.
			</p>
		</div>
	  
	
	  <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Supports USB HUB Expansion</div>
      <p class="richDesc">
				Flexible switching of USB-C / 4 × USB-A HOST ports via DIP switch
			</p>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-19.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard USB DIP switch" class="lazyload">
		</div>
	
	  <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Onboard M.2 slot for 4G Module</div>
      <p class="richDesc pdTRBL">
				The USB-A-4 port can be switched to 4G module M.2 slot via DIP switch, Supports <a href="/sim7600x-h-m2.htm" target="_blank" style="color: #ffffff;">SIM7600G-H-M.2</a> 4G module
 
			</p>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-21.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard USB / M.2 slot DIP switch" class="lazyload">
		</div>
	  
		
		<div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color:#ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Multiple Audio Interfaces</div>
      <p class="richDesc pdTRBL">
				Onboard microphone + microphone expansion header + 3.5mm audio output jack, meets a variety of audio application scenarios
			</p>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-23.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard multiple audio interfaces" class="lazyload">
		</div>
	  
	  
  	 <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000;">
    	<div class="richTitle" style="color:#ffffff;">What's On Board</div>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-intro.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, onboard components" class="lazyload">
		<div class="bgWhite round1234" style="background: #0F0B0C;">
			  <div class="alignl bgGrey round1234">
		<div class="richGridWrap richGridWrap-valignTop richGridWrap-2c alignl subBlock">
        <div>
          <ol>
            <li class="note"><strong>Core1106</strong><br>
			  			RV1106G3 / RV1106G2 core module, optional for Wi-Fi / Bluetooth wireless module</li>
            <li><strong>4G NET LED</strong><br>
			  			for indicating the operating status of the 4G module</li>
            <li><strong>USER-LED</strong><br>
			  			for indicating system operating status in the default image, programmable indicator</li>
            <li><strong>4G-RESET button</strong><br>
			  			for rebooting the 4G module</li>
            <li><strong>RESET button</strong><br>
			  			for rebooting the Core1106 system</li>
            <li><strong>BOOT button</strong><br>
            Press it when powering on or resetting to enter download mode</li>
            <li><strong>USB Type-C port</strong><br>
			  			for power supply and program burning</li>
            <li><strong>RTC battery connector</strong></li>
            <li><strong>SIM card slot</strong></li>
            <li><strong>CSI camera interface</strong><br>
            MIPI CSI 2-lane</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ol start="11">
            <li><strong>3.5mm audio jack</strong><br>
            Single channel audio output</li>
            <li><strong>Microphone expansion header</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Onboard microphone</strong></li>
            <li><strong>USB-A Host ports</strong><br>
            Expands 4x USB-A ports via USB-HUB chip</li>
            <li><strong>RJ45 100M Ethernet port</strong></li>
            <li><strong>DIP Switches</strong><br>
			 			Switch 1: for switching USB-C port and 4x USB-A ports<br>
						Switch 2: for switching  USB-A-4 port and 4G module M.2 slot</li>
            <li><strong>4G module M.2 slot</strong><br>
            Supports SIM7600G-H-M.2 4G module</li>
            <li><strong>PoE module header</strong></li>
            <li><strong>40PIN GPIO header</strong><br>
			  			Compatible with some Raspberry Pi HATs</li>
            <li><strong>TF card slot</strong><br>
			  			Supports storage expansion only</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
						</div>
		</div>
    </div>
	  
	 <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color: #ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">Pin definition</div>
		  <div><br></div>
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-inter-1.jpg" class="round1234 lazyload" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, pin definition 1">
    	<img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-inter-2.jpg" class="round1234 lazyload" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, pin definition 2">
		</div>
	  
	 <div class="pdT" style="background: #000000; color: #ffffff;">
    	<div class="richTitle">outline dimensions</div>
      <img data-src="/image/catalog/development-board/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A/Luckfox-Pico-Pi-A-details-size.jpg" alt="Luckfox Pico Pi series, outline dimensions" class="lazyload">
		
    </div>
	  <br>


	
	</div>

	
</div>
</div>
